# Execution continuity (plans / tickets / SDD)

Applies when the user has **approved** a spec/plan/tickets and chosen execution (Subagent-Driven, Inline Execution, "按 tickets 执行", "ok 继续实现", "开始 T0", etc.).

## Do

1. Run all tickets/tasks in the approved plan **serially** without stopping to ask "要继续吗？" after each one.
2. After each ticket: 1–3 sentence progress note, then **immediately** start the next ticket.
3. Pause only when: a step fails and cannot be fixed; spec/plan conflict; a genuine user decision is required (not inferable from the plan).

## Do not

- Ask "要做 Tn+1 吗？" at every ticket boundary.
- Treat a single "ok" on the execution mode as permission for **one** ticket only — it authorizes the **full** approved run unless the user narrows scope.

## End of run

Summarize: tickets completed, blockers (if any), commit SHAs (if any). Do not batch-ask "要继续吗？" mid-run.

Does **not** apply to brainstorming, design review, or ad-hoc Q&A without an approved execution plan.
